/src/main/**/generated
/src/main/jniLibs/**/*.so
/src/main/assets/tauri.conf.json
/tauri.build.gradle.kts
/proguard-tauri.pro
/tauri.properties
# Build products of `tauri android build`/`dev`. `src/main/assets/` is where the
# frontend dist and every `bundle > resources` entry are copied for packaging —
# a copy of built output, not authored content.
#
# ⚠️ 70 MB of it reached a commit before this line existed: `bundle.resources`
# in `tauri.conf.json` stages `vendor/inference/current/` as `runtime/`, so an
# Android build copied the DESKTOP macOS inference runtime — `lemond`, and the
# llama.cpp Metal `.dylib`s — into the app. The Apple template has ignored its
# own `assets/` since somebody hit the same thing there; this one shipped
# without the equivalent.
/src/main/assets/

# Compiled Rust for each Android ABI. The template above ignores `**/*.so`
# inside this directory; the directory itself is safer, because everything the
# NDK leaves here is compiler output and the next thing it leaves may not end
# in `.so` — a stripped variant, a versioned suffix, a `.a`.
/src/main/jniLibs/
